    <string name="tut_home_1_title">Your home base</string>
    <string name="tut_home_1_body">This card shows what is loaded and how much storage is free. The big button starts importing a game.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_2_title">Shortcuts</string>
    <string name="tut_home_2_body">Library, Manager and Settings are one tap away here. Games you play and favorite will fill the shelves below.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_3_title">Five keys</string>
    <string name="tut_home_3_body">Home, Library, Import, Manager and Settings. The lime line shows where you are.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_4_title">Ready to start?</string>
    <string name="tut_home_4_body">Begin with Settings > Runtimes to check that Winlator Cmod is installed. I will guide you there when you visit.</string>
    <string name="tut_import_1_title">Pick an archive</string>
    <string name="tut_import_1_body">Games usually come as ZIP, 7Z or TAR files. You will choose one from your phone here. The file picker is not ready yet, so this button stays locked for now.</string>
    <string name="tut_import_2_title">What happens next</string>
    <string name="tut_import_2_body">NexusPlay will extract the archive into a folder you choose, look for .exe files, and ask you to pick the right one. It never runs anything by itself.</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_1_title">Is Cmod installed?</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_1_body">This card shows what I found on your phone: the version, the Android requirement, and whether the app lets other apps start games.</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_2_title">Test a launch</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_2_body">In Cmod, create a shortcut for your game and export it to the frontend. Paste that .desktop file path here and tap Launch. I can tell whether Android delivered the request, but not whether the game started.</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_3_title">Need help?</string>
    <string name="tut_runtime_3_body">Open this section for step-by-step setup and the known limits, including the fact that the virtual gamepad cannot control Cmod.</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_1_title">Try the stick</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_1_body">Touch and drag here. X and Y show exactly what the stick sends, and the small plot shows the deadzone as a dashed ring.</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_2_title">Calibrate</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_2_body">Tap Calibrate, then circle the stick around its edge for four seconds. If you cannot reach the edge comfortably, your reach will count as full.</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_3_title">Tune it</string>
    <string name="tut_joystick_3_body">Sensitivity, deadzone, size and looks are below, and every change is saved automatically. This stick cannot control Cmod yet, because Cmod has its own controls.</string>
    <string name="tut_settings_1_title">Your control room</string>
    <string name="tut_settings_1_body">Language, mascot options, joystick and runtimes live here. Rows marked open work now, and rows marked soon are on the way.</string>
